  "description": "Incorporates vintage patterns, antiques, and traditional furnishings with contemporary sensibilities. Emerged as a reaction to minimalist trends, embracing maximalism with a nostalgic twist.",
  "culturalContext": "Grandmillennial style — coined by House Beautiful (2019) — revived \"granny chic\" for the 2020s: chintz and needlepoint cushions, wicker and bamboo (Granny's bamboo), skirted tables, botanical wallpaper, ruffles mixed with modern art and clean lines. Architects (Bunny Williams lineage) and Instagram (#grandmillennialhome) made it the pandemic-era comfort aesthetic; critics read it as irony-plus-sincerity, the anti-minimalism that made 2020s interiors warm again.",
